Description: v4l2m2m: try the DRM fourcc itself as the V4L2 format
 DRM and V4L2 share fourcc codes for the same memory layout (DRM XRGB8888 'XR24'
 is V4L2 XBGR32, bytes B, G, R, X). The name-based table maps XRGB8888 to V4L2
 XRGB32 ('BX24', bytes X, R, G, B), so a driver that follows the specification
 swaps red and blue. Try the identical fourcc first.
Author: Mariotaku <git@mariotaku.me>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-09
---
--- a/src/enc/h264/v4l2m2m-impl.c
+++ b/src/enc/h264/v4l2m2m-impl.c
@@ -165,6 +165,9 @@
 	if (have_v4l2_format(formats, n_formats, f)) \
 		return f
 
+	/* DRM and V4L2 share fourcc codes for the same memory layout. */
+	TRY_FORMAT(drm_format);
+
 	switch (drm_format) {
 	case DRM_FORMAT_RGBX8888:
 	case DRM_FORMAT_RGBA8888:
